Integration goes both ways: external systems can call **your** Apex.

```apex
@RestResource(urlMapping='/orders/*')
global with sharing class OrderApi {
    @HttpGet global static Order__c getOrder() { … }
    @HttpPost global static Id create(String name) { … }
}
```

- The endpoint lives at `/services/apexrest/orders/…` and requires an authenticated caller (usually an integration user via a Connected App).
- `RestContext.request` and `RestContext.response` give the URL, headers and body; return values are serialised to JSON.
- Prefer the standard REST API when it already does what you need; write Apex REST for custom operations.
